<div class="card bg-base-100 border border-base-300 shadow-sm mb-8" id="next-steps-card">
  <div class="card-body p-5">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-2 mb-2">
      <h3 class="card-title text-base-content text-lg flex items-center gap-2">
        Next Steps
      </h3>
      <% if (session.status === 'Primary Fermentation') { %>
        <% if (session.is_sugar_break_reached) { %>
          <span class="badge badge-warning text-black text-xs font-semibold px-2 py-0.5">Past 1/3 Sugar Break</span>
        <% } else { %>
          <span class="badge badge-info text-white text-xs font-semibold px-2 py-0.5">Degassing &amp; Aeration Phase</span>
        <% } %>
      <% } else if (session.status === 'Aging') { %>
        <% if (session.fining_state && session.fining_state.stage === 'kieselsol_added') { %>
          <span class="badge badge-warning text-black text-xs font-semibold px-2 py-0.5">Fining: Step 1 (Kieselsol [-])</span>
        <% } else if (session.fining_state && session.fining_state.stage === 'chitosan_ready') { %>
          <span class="badge badge-success text-white text-xs font-semibold px-2 py-0.5">Chitosan Window Open (12–24h)</span>
        <% } else if (session.fining_state && session.fining_state.stage === 'chitosan_overdue') { %>
          <span class="badge badge-warning text-black text-xs font-semibold px-2 py-0.5">Chitosan Overdue (&gt;24h)</span>
        <% } else if (session.fining_state && session.fining_state.stage === 'sediment_compacting') { %>
          <span class="badge badge-info text-white text-xs font-semibold px-2 py-0.5">Sediment Compacting (Day <%= (session.fining_state.days_compacting || 0) + 1 %>/14)</span>
        <% } else if (session.fining_state && session.fining_state.stage === 'sediment_compacted') { %>
          <span class="badge badge-success text-white text-xs font-semibold px-2 py-0.5">Sediment Compacted – Safe to Siphon</span>
        <% } else { %>
          <span class="badge bg-status-aging text-white text-xs font-semibold px-2 py-0.5">Aging &amp; Maturation</span>
        <% } %>
      <% } %>
    </div>

    <% if (session.status === 'Primary Fermentation') { %>
      <% if (!session.is_sugar_break_reached) { %>
        <!-- Pre-1/3 Break: Actionable Next Step Alert -->
        <div class="alert alert-info bg-info/10 border border-info/20 rounded-lg p-3.5 mb-3 flex items-start gap-2.5" id="actionable-next-step-alert">
          <span class="text-xl leading-none">💡</span>
          <div>
            <div class="text-sm font-bold text-base-content">
              Current SG is <%= currentSgFormatted %>. Remember to degas CO₂ and add your final nutrient dose before SG reaches <%= sugarBreakFormatted %>.
              <span style="display: none;">Current SG is <%= currentSgFormatted %>. Remember to degas CO₂ and add your final nutrient dose before SG reaches <%= sugarBreakFormatted %>.</span>
            </div>
            <div class="text-xs text-base-content/80 mt-1 leading-relaxed">
              Primary Care Tip (Days 1–5): Degas and swirl gently before adding nutrients or taking SG readings to release CO₂. During the first 3 to 5 days of primary fermentation, accumulated dissolved CO₂ is toxic to yeast and can cause foam-over ("volcano") explosions when dry additives are introduced.
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="space-y-2 text-sm text-base-content">
          <div class="flex items-start gap-2">
            <span class="text-info font-bold">1.</span>
            <span><strong>Daily Degas &amp; Aerate:</strong> Degas and aerate the batch daily before reaching this break (<%= sugarBreakFormatted %>). Oxygen is essential right now for healthy yeast cell growth and biomass building.</span>
          </div>
          <div class="flex items-start gap-2">
            <span class="text-info font-bold">2.</span>
            <span><strong>Swirl Before Additions:</strong> Swirl gently before adding staggered nutrients (SNA) or measuring SG to release dissolved gas and avoid violent foaming.</span>
          </div>
          <div class="flex items-start gap-2">
            <span class="text-info font-bold">3.</span>
            <span><strong>Approaching 1/3 Sugar Break (<%= sugarBreakFormatted %>):</strong> Monitor gravity. Aeration must stop completely as soon as SG reaches <%= sugarBreakFormatted %> to prevent oxidation during aging.</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      <% } else { %>
        <!-- Post-1/3 Break: Actionable Next Step Alert -->
        <div class="alert alert-warning bg-warning/15 border border-warning/30 rounded-lg p-3.5 mb-3 flex items-start gap-2.5" id="actionable-next-step-alert">
          <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="h-5 w-5 text-warning shrink-0 mt-0.5" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="currentColor">
            <path fill-rule="evenodd" d="M8.485 2.495c.673-1.167 2.357-1.167 3.03 0l6.28 10.875c.673 1.167-.17 2.625-1.516 2.625H3.72c-1.347 0-2.189-1.458-1.515-2.625L8.485 2.495zM10 5a.75.75 0 01.75.75v3.5a.75.75 0 01-1.5 0v-3.5A.75.75 0 0110 5zm0 9a1 1 0 100-2 1 1 0 000 2z" clip-rule="evenodd" />
          </svg>
          <div>
            <div class="text-sm font-bold text-base-content">
              1/3 Sugar Break reached (<%= sugarBreakFormatted %>)! Stop aerating and keep the vessel sealed under an airlock.
            </div>
            <div class="text-xs text-base-content/90 mt-1 leading-relaxed">
              Past 1/3 Sugar Break (<%= sugarBreakFormatted %>): Stop Aerating! Stop aerating once past the 1/3 break to prevent oxidation during aging. Yeast has completed its aerobic growth phase. Any oxygen introduced now will not benefit the yeast and will oxidize delicate honey aromatics into cardboard or stale notes.
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="space-y-2 text-sm text-base-content">
          <div class="flex items-start gap-2">
            <span class="text-warning font-bold">1.</span>
            <span><strong>Airlock Sealed:</strong> Keep the carboy firmly under airlock with minimal headspace. Avoid splashing or whipping air into the must.</span>
          </div>
          <div class="flex items-start gap-2">
            <span class="text-warning font-bold">2.</span>
            <span><strong>Gentle Swirling Only:</strong> If adding remaining nutrients, swirl very gently under airlock to release CO₂ without admitting air.</span>
          </div>
          <div class="flex items-start gap-2">
            <span class="text-warning font-bold">3.</span>
            <span><strong>Wait for Gravity Stability:</strong> Let fermentation run until completion. Look for two identical SG readings 7+ days apart to confirm primary fermentation is complete.</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      <% } %>
    <% } else if (session.status === 'Planned') { %>
      <p class="text-sm text-base-content leading-relaxed">
        Pitch yeast and record your first Specific Gravity reading to establish the Original Gravity (OG). Daily degassing and aeration begins once fermentation takes off.
      </p>
    <% } else if (session.status === 'Aging') { %>
      <% if (session.fining_state && session.fining_state.stage === 'kieselsol_added') { %>
        <!-- Stage 1: Kieselsol added, awaiting Chitosan 12-24h window -->
        <div class="alert alert-info bg-info/10 border border-info/20 rounded-lg p-3.5 mb-3 flex items-start gap-2.5" id="actionable-next-step-alert">
          <span class="text-xl leading-none">⏳</span>
          <div>
            <div class="text-sm font-bold text-base-content">
              Kieselsol [-] added <%= session.fining_state.hours_since_kieselsol %> hours ago. Wait 12–24 hours before adding Chitosan [+] (window opens in <%= session.fining_state.hours_until_chitosan_window %> hours).
            </div>
            <div class="text-xs text-base-content/80 mt-1 leading-relaxed">
              Dual-Stage Clarification: Kieselsol carries a negative (-) electrostatic charge and binds positively charged yeast proteins. Waiting 12 to 24 hours gives it time to disperse evenly through the mead before introducing positively charged Chitosan.
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="space-y-2 text-sm text-base-content">
          <div class="flex items-start gap-2">
            <span class="text-info font-bold">1.</span>
            <span><strong>Keep Carboy Sealed:</strong> Let the negative silica sol disperse without vigorous agitation.</span>
          </div>
          <div class="flex items-start gap-2">
            <span class="text-info font-bold">2.</span>
            <span><strong>Prepare Chitosan (+):</strong> When the 12–24 hour window opens in <%= session.fining_state.hours_until_chitosan_window %> hours, add Chitosan to complete charge neutralization and initiate flocculation.</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      <% } else if (session.fining_state && session.fining_state.stage === 'chitosan_ready') { %>
        <!-- Stage 1b: Chitosan window open (12-24h) -->
        <div class="alert alert-success bg-success/15 border border-success/30 rounded-lg p-3.5 mb-3 flex items-start gap-2.5" id="actionable-next-step-alert">
          <span class="text-xl leading-none">✨</span>
          <div>
            <div class="text-sm font-bold text-base-content">
              Optimal Window Open! It has been <%= session.fining_state.hours_since_kieselsol %> hours since Kieselsol was added (<%= session.fining_state.hours_remaining_in_chitosan_window %> hours remaining in the 12–24h window). Add Chitosan [+] now!
            </div>
            <div class="text-xs text-base-content/80 mt-1 leading-relaxed">
              Adding Chitosan (+) creates strong electrostatic bridges with the Kieselsol-coated particles, forming dense flocs that precipitate rapidly to the bottom and start the 7–14 day sediment compaction countdown.
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="space-y-2 text-sm text-base-content">
          <div class="flex items-start gap-2">
            <span class="text-success font-bold">1.</span>
            <span><strong>Add Chitosan (+):</strong> Pour in Chitosan and stir or swirl gently for 30 seconds to disperse without introducing oxygen.</span>
          </div>
          <div class="flex items-start gap-2">
            <span class="text-success font-bold">2.</span>
            <span><strong>Begin Compaction Countdown:</strong> Once Chitosan is added, leave the vessel still to begin the 7–14 day sediment bed compaction timer.</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      <% } else if (session.fining_state && session.fining_state.stage === 'chitosan_overdue') { %>
        <!-- Stage 1c: Chitosan overdue (>24h) -->
        <div class="alert alert-warning bg-warning/15 border border-warning/30 rounded-lg p-3.5 mb-3 flex items-start gap-2.5" id="actionable-next-step-alert">
          <span class="text-xl leading-none">⚠️</span>
          <div>
            <div class="text-sm font-bold text-base-content">
              Chitosan window overdue: <%= session.fining_state.hours_since_kieselsol %> hours have elapsed since Kieselsol addition. Add Chitosan [+] as soon as possible.
            </div>
            <div class="text-xs text-base-content/90 mt-1 leading-relaxed">
              Kieselsol has settled. Adding Chitosan (+) now will complete charge neutralization and bind any remaining suspended particles into tight sediment.
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="space-y-2 text-sm text-base-content">
          <div class="flex items-start gap-2">
            <span class="text-warning font-bold">1.</span>
            <span><strong>Add Chitosan (+):</strong> Add your dose of Chitosan and swirl very gently to mix.</span>
          </div>
          <div class="flex items-start gap-2">
            <span class="text-warning font-bold">2.</span>
            <span><strong>Re-seal Airlock:</strong> Seal and place in a cool location to begin sediment compaction.</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      <% } else if (session.fining_state && session.fining_state.stage === 'sediment_compacting') { %>
        <!-- Stage 2: Sediment Compaction Countdown (Days 0-13) -->
        <div class="mb-3 flex items-start gap-2.5" id="actionable-next-step-alert">
          <div>
            <div class="text-sm font-bold text-base-content">
              Sediment Compaction Countdown: Day <%= (session.fining_state.days_compacting || 0) + 1 %> of 14 (<%= session.fining_state.days_remaining_to_compact %> days remaining until full compaction).
            </div>
            <div class="text-xs text-base-content/80 mt-1 leading-relaxed">
              <% if (session.fining_state.sediment_phase === 'loose') { %>
                <strong>Loose Sediment Bed (<em>løst bunnfall</em>):</strong> During Days 1–6, flocs precipitate into a soft, fluffy layer at the bottom. Do NOT siphon or move the vessel yet — siphoning from a loose bed will draw haze directly into your bottles.
              <% } else { %>
                <strong>Compacting Bed (<em>sedimentkomprimering</em>):</strong> Between Days 7 and 14, gravity and electrostatic cohesion pull the sediment cake tight against the glass. Waiting the full 14 days guarantees maximum firmness and a crystal-clear pour.
              <% } %>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Compaction Progress Bar -->
        <div class="bg-base-200/80 rounded-lg p-3 border border-base-300 mb-3">
          <div class="flex justify-between text-xs text-pollen mb-1 font-medium">
            <span>Day 1: Flocculation</span>
            <span>Day 7: Loose Bed Settled</span>
            <span>Day 14: Tight Compaction</span>
          </div>
          <progress class="progress progress-secondary w-full" value="<%= session.fining_state.compaction_progress_pct %>" max="100"></progress>
          <div class="flex justify-between text-xs mt-1">
            <span class="text-secondary font-semibold"><%= session.fining_state.compaction_progress_pct %>% Compacted</span>
            <span class="text-pollen"><%= session.fining_state.days_remaining_to_compact %> days to safe siphoning</span>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="space-y-2 text-sm text-base-content">
          <div class="flex items-start gap-2">
            <span class="text-info font-bold">1.</span>
            <span><strong>Keep Carboy Completely Still:</strong> Any jostling or lifting will kick up the fluffy sediment bed. If moving is necessary, move 24–48 hours before siphoning.</span>
          </div>
          <div class="flex items-start gap-2">
            <span class="text-info font-bold">2.</span>
            <span><strong>Cold Crashing (Optional):</strong> Chilling the vessel to 2–4°C accelerates compaction and tightens the sediment layer even faster.</span>
          </div>
          <div class="flex items-start gap-2">
            <span class="text-info font-bold">3.</span>
            <span><strong>Wait for Day 14:</strong> Siphoning is recommended when the sediment is firmly compacted to prevent pulling yeast into the final bottles.</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      <% } else if (session.fining_state && session.fining_state.stage === 'sediment_compacted') { %>
        <!-- Stage 3: Sediment fully compacted (Day 14+) -->
        <div class="alert alert-success bg-success/15 border border-success/30 rounded-lg p-3.5 mb-3 flex items-start gap-2.5" id="actionable-next-step-alert">
          <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="h-5 w-5 text-success shrink-0 mt-0.5" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="currentColor">
            <path fill-rule="evenodd" d="M10 18a8 8 0 100-16 8 8 0 000 16zm3.707-9.293a1 1 0 00-1.414-1.414L9 10.586 7.707 9.293a1 1 0 00-1.414 1.414l2 2a1 1 0 001.414 0l4-4z" clip-rule="evenodd" />
          </svg>
          <div>
            <div class="text-sm font-bold text-base-content">
              Sediment Bed Compacted (<em>kompakt bunnfall</em>)! Safe to siphon into bottles.
            </div>
            <div class="text-xs text-base-content/90 mt-1 leading-relaxed">
              14+ days of compaction have locked the yeast and protein sediment into a dense, solid cake at the bottom of the vessel. You can now siphon clear mead without drawing haze into the final pour.
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="space-y-2 text-sm text-base-content">
          <div class="flex items-start gap-2">
            <span class="text-success font-bold">1.</span>
            <span><strong>Sanitize Siphoning Gear:</strong> Prepare your auto-siphon, tubing, and sanitized bottles.</span>
          </div>
          <div class="flex items-start gap-2">
            <span class="text-success font-bold">2.</span>
            <span><strong>Siphon Above the Bed:</strong> Rest the siphon cap slightly above the tight sediment bed. Stop when liquid nears the cake to maintain pure clarity.</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      <% } else { %>
        <!-- Baseline Aging without fining -->
        <div class="space-y-2 text-sm text-base-content">
          <p class="leading-relaxed">
            Batch is aging (<em>modning</em>). Keep vessel topped up and airlock intact to prevent oxidation.
          </p>
          <div class="bg-base-200/50 rounded-lg p-3 border border-base-300 text-xs text-pollen">
            💡 <strong>Clarification Tip:</strong> If your mead is cloudy from suspended yeast and proteins after fermentation, use a two-component clarifier like <strong>Super-Kleer (Kieselsol [-] + Chitosan [+])</strong>. Adding Kieselsol first followed by Chitosan 12–24 hours later drops haze and starts the 7–14 day sediment compaction countdown for haze-free bottling.
          </div>
        </div>
      <% } %>
    <% } else if (session.status === 'Bottled') { %>
      <p class="text-sm text-base-content leading-relaxed">
        Batch is bottled! Store in a cool, dark place to mature.
      </p>
    <% } %>
  </div>
</div>
